From: ship/bootstrap delegation -- the three protected delegated skills
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): drop disable-model-invocation from the protected delegated skills

Human-applied patch. These three SKILL.md files are registered protected gate
artifacts; the other 17 delegated skills in the same change were edited
directly.

Each already carries `user-invocable: false`, which keeps a human from starting
it out of order. Carrying `disable-model-invocation: true` as well left it
reachable by NOBODY -- not a human, not the model -- so ship and bootstrap
could never delegate to their lower stages. Removing the key is the Codex
plugin's own shape for internal skills: `user-invocable: false` and no
`disable-model-invocation` key at all.

Until this is applied, tests/validate-repository.ps1 throws on exactly these
three files. That is the corrected gate working, not a regression.

Verify, then apply:
    git apply --check reports/notes/skill-delegation-protected-three.patch
    git apply reports/notes/skill-delegation-protected-three.patch
    pwsh -NoProfile -File tests/validate-repository.ps1

